==Strategy==
*In order to beat this stage, you must bring spammable cats ([[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank]] are the best choices). The Dragon Cats ([[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Normal]] and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed]]) both [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion Cat]] and [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Giraffe Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] (After killing Mega Cat) and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], if available.
*Bring your anti-Floating Massive Damage Cats, such as [[Archer Cat (Rare Cat)|Cataur]] or [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]] to deal with the high health of the Vlad de Sables and Count Owlbrows. Anti-Dark units aren't necessary, as the Vlad de Sables and Count Owlbrows aren't classed as Dark enemies. '''Do not bring any Cats that inflict knockback, as your cats will progress into Mega Cat's range and be wiped out.''' At least three meatshields are needed and they need to be spammed, as Mega Cat will occasionally nuke the playing field, destroying anything that can't tank a hit. [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] can survive the attack, but he is a poor choice on this stage, as the Vlad de Sables and Pumpkin Doges will break him down quickly. [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] can also tank a hit, and is more practical due to his lower cost and recharge.
*You can get free hits on the Mega Cat when it first spawns by spawning the Giraffe Cats before being annihilated by the Mega Cat or the Vlad de Sables. After that when the Count Owlbrows spawn, start spawning both Dragon Cats and fend them off until they are all defeated and the Vlad de Sable horde dies down. Afterwards, spawn Lion Cats and Crazed Giraffe Cats and after killing the Mega Cat the stage should be a breeze as the stage will only spawn the Pumpkin Doges and the Firework Guys. This is the part where you can now use your heavy hitters (Bahamut) to damage the base.
*Keep your damage-dealers safe to deal with the Vlad de Sables and Count Owlbrows, and the stage becomes much easier. While Mega Cat is very powerful, it is classed as a Metal enemy with very low health, which means that it can be defeated easily by a swarm of Lion Cats and Crazed Giraffe Cats. Sending [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]] in-between Mega Cat's cooldowns can take it out quickly.
*A way to make the stage significantly easier is to send out Catornado accompanied by Crazed Giraffe and/or Lion Cat after Mega Cat's first attack. The lions and giraffes will defend Catornado from any Vlad de Sables that might appear. If your timing is right, Catornado can attack and kill Mega Cat, making the battle much more manageable. [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]] (normal form only) may also be effective, due to crits and long range.
* If you have [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan Pasalan]], you can just stay defensive until he attacks, one-shotting Mega Cat, then complete the level normally. E. Kubilan's wave attack outranges the boss, so he can stay safe out of his range while attacking.

